Spec: children

Purpose:
  Assemble one package instance's child inventory together with live cluster state for the
    diagnostic API's `children` endpoint: read the requested instance CRD by kind, flatten every
    @Children record out of all child-carrying `status` categories from its serialized form, then
    for each child fetch its live Kubernetes object for the five supported kinds, anonymize it
    through @scrub_json, and build one @ChildWithState per child plus the payload-wide redaction
    tally. A failed child-object read degrades that entry to a null @state without failing the
    call; a failed instance read or a failed scrub aborts the whole call.

Owns:
  ./children.rs

References:
  ./dto.sdd — @ChildWithState and @ScrubStats are this file's output types; their wire shapes and
    the `X-Diag-Redactions` header coupling live there.
  ./error.sdd — the exit lane: only @DiagError::UnknownKind, @DiagError::KubeError and
    @DiagError::SerializationError ever leave this file; their statuses and ids are owned there.
  ./anonymize.sdd — the @scrub_json contract: value/regex masking, per-call Secret listing over
    both namespaces, and the @serde_json::@Error lane this file's `?` converts to
    @DiagError::SerializationError.
  ./state.sdd — the client arriving as the @get_children argument is the @AppState.client handle
    cloned by ./server.rs; the server identity whose RBAC decides which child reads fail is
    specified there.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd, /common/src/instanceservice.sdd, /common/src/instancesystem.sdd —
    the CRD models read here: which `status` keys hold @crate::Children lists per kind, and
    `services` holding @crate::Published instead.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — the @Children wire gate (`kind` and `name` required) that
    @extract_children_from_json accepts or rejects by.

Must:
  Kind dispatch is exact and case-sensitive on the three lowercase plurals `tenantinstances`,
    `serviceinstances`, `systeminstances`; every other @kind string returns
    @DiagError::UnknownKind before this file issues any cluster read.
  All cluster reads are point reads: one @Api::namespaced + @Api::get of `name` in `namespace` for
    the instance, one @Api::get of @Children::name per child — no `list`, no `watch`, no
    @ListParams, no label or field selector exists anywhere in this file (the Secret lists happen
    inside @scrub_json, owned by ./anonymize.rs).
  Child extraction is kind-agnostic and JSON-driven: after the typed read the instance is
    serialized and the seven @CHILD_CATEGORIES keys are read in declaration order — `befores`,
    `vitals`, `scalables`, `others`, `posts`, `systems`, `services` — each category only when
    present and an array, each entry only when it deserializes as @Children; `crds` is not a
    category and an absent or non-object `status` yields zero children.
  The seven-category union serves all three CRDs from one code path — `systems` is
    @SystemInstance-only and the in-file comment pins that omitting it once dropped every
    @SystemInstance child — yet extraction never filters by the read kind: a tenant `status`
    carrying a `systems` array, or a system `status` carrying `befores`, is read just the same.
  Child-state lookup dispatches on the exact @Children::kind strings `Deployment`,
    `StatefulSet`, `DaemonSet`, `Service`, `ConfigMap`; group and version are hardcoded by the
    @k8s_openapi types (@api::apps::v1 for the first three, @api::core::v1 for the last two) and
    @Children::api_version is never consulted, so a child declared in another group is fetched
    from the hardcoded one.
  Per-child fetch scope: the namespace is @Children::namespace when @Some — the empty string
    included, used verbatim — otherwise the instance `namespace`; an successfully fetched object
    is handed to @scrub_json with that resolved child namespace plus the caller's
    `vynil_namespace`, and its masked @serde_json::@Value becomes @ChildWithState::state.
  Every extracted child yields exactly one @ChildWithState { child, state } in output order —
    category-declaration order, then in-array order; status duplicates produce duplicate entries,
    and no step ever dedupes or drops the child itself, even when its state is lost.
  A child-object read failing with any @kube::Error — `404`, RBAC `403`, decode — or a kind
    outside the five known kinds degrades to @None state plus @ScrubStats::default() and the call
    still completes @Ok with every other child assembled.
  The tally is exactly sum: per child @ScrubStats::distinct and @ScrubStats::occurrences are
    folded in with @saturating_add, so degraded and unknown-kind children contribute zeroes and
    the returned @ScrubStats describes the full returned payload.
  This file owns no cache, TTL, informer or global state: every @get_children call re-reads the
    instance, re-reads every child and re-collects secrets (one @scrub_json Secret sweep per
    masked child, per ./anonymize.sdd); children are processed sequentially in output order, and
    the first hard failure anywhere aborts the whole call.

Depends on:
  @kube `3.1.0` — @kube::Client and @kube::@api::Api (versions locked in /Cargo.lock); only the
    @namespaced constructor and @get are used, and the client is cloned per @Api build.
  @k8s_openapi `0.27.1` — @Deployment, @StatefulSet, @DaemonSet, @Service, @ConfigMap as the five
    fetchable child types and their hardcoded group/version.
  @crate::anonymize::scrub_json in ./anonymize.rs — the mask-and-tally step every successfully
    fetched child passes through.
  @crate::dto::@ChildWithState and @crate::dto::@ScrubStats in ./dto.rs — output shapes, with
    @ScrubStats::default as the degraded-entry and accumulator seed.
  @crate::error::@DiagError in ./error.rs — the return lane, plus the @From-derived
    @DiagError::SerializationError conversion the `?` legs use.
  @common — @Children from /common/src/lib.rs and the @TenantInstance, @ServiceInstance,
    @SystemInstance CRDs from /common/src/instancetenant.rs, /common/src/instanceservice.rs,
    /common/src/instancesystem.rs.
  @serde_json — @to_value of instance and fetched object, @from_value per category entry;
    @serde::Serialize is the generic bound @extract_children_from_instance serializes through.

Exposes:
  Full public surface — `pub mod children;` in ./collect/mod.rs under `pub mod collect;` in
    /server/src/lib.rs; consumers are ./server.rs (`children` endpoint, via
    `@crate::collect::children::get_children`) and ./logs.rs (@get_instance_children over
    @all_children_from_status):
  @get_children — `pub async fn @get_children(client: &@kube::Client, kind: &@str, namespace:
    &@str, name: &@str, vynil_namespace: &@str) -> @Result<(Vec<@ChildWithState>, @ScrubStats),
    @DiagError>`; the complete instance-children assembly, doc-commented to fail with
    @DiagError::UnknownKind or the Kubernetes/serialization error of a failing read.
  @all_children_from_status — `#[must_use] pub fn @all_children_from_status(instance_json:
    &@serde_json::@Value) -> Vec<@Children>`; the shared category flattener reused by ./logs.rs so
    both collectors flatten identically.
  Everything else is private to this module: @get_tenant_children, @get_service_children and
    @get_system_children (`async fn` each, same `(&@kube::Client, &@str, &@str) ->
    @Result<Vec<@Children>, @DiagError>` shape), @CHILD_CATEGORIES (the seven literals),
    @extract_children_from_instance (over `&(impl @serde::Serialize + @std::fmt::Debug)`),
    @extract_children_from_json and @get_child_state (returning
    `@Result<(Option<@serde_json::@Value>, @ScrubStats), @DiagError>`).

Accepts:
  @get_children takes a live borrowed @kube::Client plus four free-form @str borrows: `kind` is
    matched raw against the three plurals (./server.rs restricts it and validates DNS forms
    upstream, but this function re-gates `kind` and validates nothing else), `namespace` and `name`
    go verbatim into the instance get and the child-namespace fallback, `vynil_namespace` reaches
    only @scrub_json as the second Secret-collection namespace.
  @all_children_from_status accepts any @serde_json::@Value; only a `status` key that is an object
    is ever inspected.
  No instance shape is preconditioned: missing `status`, all-absent categories and empty arrays
    are ordinary @Ok inputs yielding an empty inventory.

Returns:
  @Ok of `(Vec<@ChildWithState>, @ScrubStats)` — one entry per extracted child, in the order fixed
    under `Must`, @state @Some(scrubbed object) for fetched-and-masked children and @None
    otherwise, the tally summed over all of them; ./server.rs renders the vector as the `200`
    `application/json` body and the tally into `X-Diag-Redactions` (./dto.sdd), where @None
    serializes as an explicit `"state":null` key.
  An instance with no children returns an empty vector with an all-zero @ScrubStats, not an error
    — the endpoint answers `200` with `[]`.
  @all_children_from_status returns a possibly-empty Vec and never fails.

Raises:
  @DiagError::UnknownKind — any `kind` outside the three plurals, raised before any cluster call.
  @DiagError::KubeError — every @kube::Error from the instance get in @get_tenant_children,
    @get_service_children or @get_system_children, mapped explicitly by
    `@map_err(@DiagError::KubeError)`; the call @Errs whole — a Kubernetes-side `404` for a
    vanished instance (racing ./server.rs's existence pre-check) still travels as `500`-lane
    @DiagError::KubeError, never as @DiagError::InstanceNotFound (./error.sdd).
  @DiagError::SerializationError — from @get_child_state only: @serde_json::to_value of a fetched
    child object failing, or @scrub_json @Err (masked text no longer re-parsing, ./anonymize.sdd);
    `?` aborts the call discarding the vector already built — no partial inventory is ever
    delivered.
  Not raised here, despite touching this data path: child-get failures, entry-level @serde_json
    rejects and the instance-serialization fallback all stay internal (Handles).

Handles:
  Child read failures in bulk — objects deleted after recording, RBAC refused, name drifted: the
    consumer sees the child with `"state":null` and no reason; deleted, forbidden and
    never-fetchable entries are indistinguishable on the wire.
  Unsupported child kinds — `Pod`, `Job`, `Secret`, lowercase `deployment`, anything — short-circuit
    to @None with zero stats and zero cluster calls.
  Status-shape drift — a category holding a non-array, or entries of the @Published shape the
    typed contract actually stores under `services`, fails the @Children gate and is dropped
    silently by @extract_children_from_json's @filter_map.
  Instance serialization failure — @extract_children_from_instance's @unwrap_or_default turns it
    into zero children and a normal run (the doc comment calls the failure unrealistic; Tasks).
  Mid-run abort — the n-th child failing @scrub_json discards children 1..n-1 that were already
    masked and tallied.

Tasks:
  [ ] No `#[cfg(test)]` module exists in this file and the server crate has no integration test
      files today; cover all Scenarios below from these blocks under the project TTD rule once a
      cluster double exists (the server crate's dev-dependencies are empty, per ./anonymize.sdd).
  [?] @Children::api_version is ignored by child dispatch — all five fetches use the group/version
      hardcoded in the @k8s_openapi types, and the in-file comment concedes a "simplified
      approach"; e.g. a child declared `mygroup/v1/Service` is fetched from @api::core::v1 and
      then degrades to @None. Decide later whether api_version routes dispatch.
  [?] The `services` category is typed @Vec<@crate::Published> in both CRDs that carry it, a
      @Published object never passes the @Children gate, and @Published::definition is nested and
      never read — so the category yields children only for hand-authored or legacy-shaped
      status. Decide later whether it stays, goes, or flattens `definition`.
  [?] Child-read swallowing is total: `404`, RBAC `403` and decode errors alike land as
      `"state":null` with no reason on the wire and no log line — a server missing get-RBAC on the
      five kinds reads to clients as "every child vanished". Decide later whether per-child status
      belongs on the wire.
  [?] Instance-serialization failure silently yields zero children via @unwrap_or_default instead
      of @DiagError::SerializationError; the doc comment argues the failure is unreachable.
      Decide later whether it propagates.
  [?] Sequential N+1 with no cache or consistency snapshot: per request the file issues 1 instance
      get plus up to 1 child get and 2 Secret lists (@scrub_json's sweep) per fetched child, so a
      30-child instance costs ~90 round trips with a window in which the inventory can drift.
      Decide later whether batching, caching or a snapshot belongs here.
  [?] Extraction is kind-agnostic, so foreign categories on a written-back status are honoured
      (a `systems` array on a @TenantInstance ships as children); the fix-of-record comment froze
      the union deliberately. Decide later whether categories should be filtered per kind.
  [?] The doc comment of @get_children says it returns the Kubernetes/serialization error raised
      "while reading the instance and its children", but child-get errors never propagate —
      only scrub/serialize ones do. Reconcile wording with the degradation contract.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test in `server`, the `[?]` decisions above are recorded,
    and `cargo test -p server` with `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and
    `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stays green.

Scenario: Kind routes, everything else fails pre-call
  Given @get_children with kind `systeminstances`
  When it runs
  Then exactly one namespaced @Api::get of the @SystemInstance by `name` in `namespace` is issued
    and extraction reads that JSON's categories
  Given kind `TenantInstances` with a capital T, or `pods`, or `""`
  Then @DiagError::UnknownKind is returned and no cluster read happens at all
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Categories flatten in declaration order across one status
  Given a @TenantInstance status holding `befores` [A,B], `posts` [C] and a foreign `systems` [D]
    of @Children-shaped entries, plus a `services` array holding one @Published-shaped object
  When @all_children_from_status runs
  Then the vector is A, B, C, D — category order `befores`/`vitals`/`scalables`/`others`/`posts`/
    `systems`/`services`, in-array order within each
  And the @Published-shaped entry contributes nothing — missing `kind`/`name` drops it silently
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Child namespace wins, instance namespace falls back
  Given a child with @Children::namespace `tenant-a` while the instance `namespace` is `team-a`
  When @get_child_state runs for it
  Then the object get is namespaced to `tenant-a` and @scrub_json receives `tenant-a`, not `team-a`
  And a child with @None namespace is instead fetched — and scrubbed — in `team-a`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Missing child degrades to a null state, response still completes
  Given an instance whose recorded `Deployment` child object returns `404` from its get while a
    second child fetches fine
  When @get_children runs
  Then the call @Oks with both entries present, the missing one carrying @None @state and adding
    zeroes to the tally, and only the fetched child's stats summed
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Unsupported child kind costs zero calls
  Given a recorded child of kind `Job`
  When @get_child_state runs
  Then no API request is made for it and the result is (@None, @ScrubStats::default())
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Scrub abort discards the partial inventory
  Given two children where the first masks cleanly and the second's masked text no longer
    re-parses as JSON
  When @get_children runs
  Then @Err(@DiagError::SerializationError) is returned — the first child's already-built
    @ChildWithState is discarded and the caller receives no partial list
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Instance read failure fails the whole call
  Given the kind-matched instance get failing (deleted mid-request, or RBAC-refined)
  When @get_children runs
  Then the call @Errs as @DiagError::KubeError with no vector at all — contrasting the child lane,
    which never fails the call
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Hostile status shapes are total, not fatal
  Given JSON values with no `status`, a `status` that is a string, and @Children-shaped objects
    stored under unlisted keys such as `crds`
  When @all_children_from_status runs
  Then each yields an empty Vec — only the seven listed keys of an object `status`, only when they
    carry arrays, are ever read
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  A `Deployment` child plus an unsupported `Job` child render from ./server.rs as
    `[{"child":{"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","name":"web","namespace":"tenant-a"},"state":{ …masked object… }}`
    plus `{"child":{"apiVersion":"batch/v1","kind":"Job","name":"hook","namespace":null},"state":null}`
    — the `Job` never reaches the cluster, so its @None namespace fallback to the instance
    namespace is never even consumed
  Both counters saturate: @ScrubStats::default() folded per child keeps `distinct=0;occurrences=0`
    when every child degraded — the endpoint still answers `200` with that header
